Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:17:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Patch into an empty or flow-style parent without breaking the
 config

Patch inserts a new key by splicing text below its parent, which assumes the
parent is a block mapping. A parent written as `streams: {}` or `streams: null`
has no block: the text lands after it and the result no longer parses, so
PUT /api/streams answers 400 "did not find expected key" or "mapping values
are not allowed in this context" and the stream is never saved.

Both forms are what re-encoding the config writes for an empty map - PATCH
/api/config does exactly that - so deleting the last stream and then patching
the config leaves `streams: null`, and the next stream cannot be added.

Such a parent is now rewritten whole as a block mapping, holding what it held
plus the new key, or minus a removed one. A bare `streams:` keeps the existing
path, which already handled it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
